{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguLs4n7Ec1MtTqFpzbqB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309842,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c085d9a-8c1d-4329-8588-fab9897b1131","uuid":"efbad94f-66b0-48a2-ac28-42361d4a0ad5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T13:41:19.130Z","thinking_duration_ms":1573,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguLs4n7Ec1MtTqFpzbqB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016ePaRefKGKtjdUN16i34Tb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/report.md","content":"# A seasonal, event-aware volatility model for Synth SN50 — campaign-7 report\n\n*Audience: Synth miners. Everything here was measured with synth-lib's own scorer\n(`score_crps` / `backtest`), on the validator's real prompt times, over the frozen snapshot\n(2025-08-01 → 2026-11-08). Lower CRPS is better.*\n\n## 1. Context\n\nA Synth miner answers a prompt `(asset, start_time, horizon)` with 1000 simulated price paths. The\nvalidator scores the fan with CRPS on many interval returns at once:\n\n| configuration | what is summed (each a CRPS in basis points) | share of our CRPS |\n|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H / COM_EQU_24H (5-min steps, 289 points) | 288 5-min returns, 48 30-min returns, 8 3-h returns, the final price | 61% / 25% / 11% / 4% |\n| CRYPTO_1H (1-min steps, 61 points) | 60 1-min, 30 2-min, 12 5-min, 4 15-min, 2 30-min returns, final price, 12 \"gap\" returns from the start (5..60 min), plus a volatility term | 26 / 19 / 12 / 7 / 5 / 3.5 / 28 / 1 % |\n\nTwo consequences drive everything below:\n\n1. In the 24h configurations, **60% of the score is the 288 individual 5-minute returns**. What\n   matters most is the per-step volatility *profile* over the day, not the 24-hour total.\n2. In the 1h configuration, the very short returns and the cumulative \"gap\" returns dominate,\n   so the **current** volatility (the last tens of minutes) is what counts.\n\n## 2. Approach\n\nA closed-form, CPU-only model (≈50 ms per 24h prompt, ≈25 ms per 1h prompt, no weights):\n\n1. **Weekly volatility profile keyed on New York time** (minute of the week, 10,080 buckets, per\n   asset), fitted offline on the snapshot. Keying on New York (not UTC) keeps the US open, the\n   08:30 releases and the 16:00 close in place across daylight-saving switches. The profile is a\n   *robust* shape (mean absolute return per bucket, squared), smoothed ±4 min, with the\n   minute-of-hour pattern restored (the first minute of each hour/half-hour is 20-25% more active),\n   and fitted with scheduled-event windows excluded.\n2. **Level**: three EWMAs (fast / medium / slow) of the deseasonalised absolute returns found in\n   the context, mixed with weights that depend on the lead time (HAR-style term structure).\n3. **Scheduled events** from the calendar the miner receives (CPI, NFP, PPI, retail sales,\n   GDP/PCE, FOMC, earnings): a variance multiplier for each window after the release, fitted as\n   the median effect of past releases of the same type.\n4. **Paths**: Student-t(5) innovations × a per-path log-normal variance multiplier (the level is\n   uncertain), plus exactly-zero steps at the profiled share (stale minutes are real).\n\n*(Sections 3-6 are completed at the end of the campaign.)*\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309842,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c085d9a-8c1d-4329-8588-fab9897b1131","uuid":"51c4ff61-44eb-4302-bfe2-592bc0fcd59a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T13:41:30.048Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ePaRefKGKtjdUN16i34Tb","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/agent/report.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c085d9a-8c1d-4329-8588-fab9897b1131","uuid":"603506d1-2194-4359-b262-2e01c3ac5f0b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T13:41:30.075Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/workspace/agent/report.md","content":"# A seasonal, event-aware volatility model for Synth SN50 — campaign-7 report\n\n*Audience: Synth miners. Everything here was measured with synth-lib's own scorer\n(`score_crps` / `backtest`), on the validator's real prompt times, over the frozen snapshot\n(2025-08-01 → 2026-11-08). Lower CRPS is better.*\n\n## 1. Context\n\nA Synth miner answers a prompt `(asset, start_time, horizon)` with 1000 simulated price paths. The\nvalidator scores the fan with CRPS on many interval returns at once:\n\n| configuration | what is summed (each a CRPS in basis points) | share of our CRPS |\n|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H / COM_EQU_24H (5-min steps, 289 points) | 288 5-min returns, 48 30-min returns, 8 3-h returns, the final price | 61% / 25% / 11% / 4% |\n| CRYPTO_1H (1-min steps, 61 points) | 60 1-min, 30 2-min, 12 5-min, 4 15-min, 2 30-min returns, final price, 12 \"gap\" returns from the start (5..60 min), plus a volatility term | 26 / 19 / 12 / 7 / 5 / 3.5 / 28 / 1 % |\n\nTwo consequences drive everything below:\n\n1. In the 24h configurations, **60% of the score is the 288 individual 5-minute returns**. What\n   matters most is the per-step volatility *profile* over the day, not the 24-hour total.\n2. In the 1h configuration, the very short returns and the cumulative \"gap\" returns dominate,\n   so the **current** volatility (the last tens of minutes) is what counts.\n\n## 2. Approach\n\nA closed-form, CPU-only model (≈50 ms per 24h prompt, ≈25 ms per 1h prompt, no weights):\n\n1. **Weekly volatility profile keyed on New York time** (minute of the week, 10,080 buckets, per\n   asset), fitted offline on the snapshot. Keying on New York (not UTC) keeps the US open, the\n   08:30 releases and the 16:00 close in place across daylight-saving switches. The profile is a\n   *robust* shape (mean absolute return per bucket, squared), smoothed ±4 min, with the\n   minute-of-hour pattern restored (the first minute of each hour/half-hour is 20-25% more active),\n   and fitted with scheduled-event windows excluded.\n2. **Level**: three EWMAs (fast / medium / slow) of the deseasonalised absolute returns found in\n   the context, mixed with weights that depend on the lead time (HAR-style term structure).\n3. **Scheduled events** from the calendar the miner receives (CPI, NFP, PPI, retail sales,\n   GDP/PCE, FOMC, earnings): a variance multiplier for each window after the release, fitted as\n   the median effect of past releases of the same type.\n4. **Paths**: Student-t(5) innovations × a per-path log-normal variance multiplier (the level is\n   uncertain), plus exactly-zero steps at the profiled share (stale minutes are real).\n\n*(Sections 3-6 are completed at the end of the campaign.)*\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016ePaRefKGKtjdUN16i34Tb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
