riday session (last-6h rms 10 bp) inflated the level, and the\nweekend does not follow it.\n- weekend steps use slow-heavy EWMA weights ([0,.3,.7] or [0,0,1]) for every prompt: A com-equ\n  +0.06/+0.15%, crypto +0.56/+1.43%; B +0.05/+0.13%, crypto +0.01/+0.05%; C -0.02/-0.05%. Much\n  worse: inside a weekend, the weekend's own recent minutes are the best information. Discard.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Prepare official eval scripts and starter copy; journal"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":348737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1041,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c085d9a-8c1d-4329-8588-fab9897b1131","uuid":"461da6aa-4e71-4ec8-9eec-f33c49f28ee1","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:10:36.380Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ykLPkABVncvKVtakWKrXV","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c085d9a-8c1d-4329-8588-fab9897b1131","uuid":"6a591694-23c3-4026-8b5d-a979aaeba59e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:10:36.617Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/research/starter_eval/predict.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":338,"lines":["+\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.","+","+Usage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15","+Answers, with agent/modeling.py, the prompts the validator scored in the --days before --eval-end,","+at the start times it actually used (read from the offline field bundle), then scores them with","+backtest() (validator CRPS + rank vs the real field, from the same bundle). A prompt is scored one","+horizon after it starts, so generation begins one horizon before the scored days.","+--cadence-minutes N answers an even grid over the same span instead; each scored prompt is then","+answered by the grid point at or before it.","+","+--crps-only scores CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid (--cadence-minutes,","+by default every 60 minutes for 24h prompts and every 10 for 1h, on the round hour): no field, no","+rank, and any window of the snapshot, including before the bundle's span. Compare models on the same","+grid with it; it is not an absolute calibration level. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula.","+","+Works on every asset. A minute without a trade is a flat candle with trade_count 0. Prices load","+through the same lenient path the scored evaluation uses, so a NaN close (no price at all) reaches","+simulate() rather than stopping the run — your model must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate).","+The context spans the CONTEXT_DAYS your modeling.py sets (7 without it), and the days before an","+asset's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day, are NaN.","+","+When the snapshot carries an event calendar ($SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR), the summary is followed by","+your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type and","+over those that hold none: where an event costs you, that gap is wider.","+","+--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size","+(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up","+generation at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for","+fewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.","+","+The context a prompt gets ends BEFORE its start_time, and that is not an off-by-one. The store","+labels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t closes at t+60s — and that close is","+the first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is","+scored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to","+its own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.","+\"\"\"","+","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import argparse","+import json","+import os","+import shutil","+import sys","+import tempfile","+from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone","+from pathlib import Path","+","+import numpy as np","+import pandas as pd","+","+from synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES","+from synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores","+from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps","+from synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (","+    context_days_of,","+    context_slice,","+    load_minute_prices,","+    nan_head_minutes,","+)","+from synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR","+from synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns","+","+# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the","+# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)","+# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.","+AGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent","+WORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parents[2]  # this copy lives in agent/research/starter_eval/","+sys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))","+","+import modeling  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)","+","+# Your modeling.py's CONTEXT_DAYS, read as the verdict and the live miner read it.","+CONTEXT_DAYS = context_days_of(modeling)","+# Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one.","+PREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"","+# Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR.","+OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV = \"SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT\"","+# backtest()'s default miner_id: the rows of prompt_df that are yours.","+CANDIDATE_ID = 999","+# The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES.","+CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}","+","+","+def ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:","+    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.","+","+    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via","+    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves","+    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find","+    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted","+    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"","+    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)","+","+","+def require_offline_bundle() -> None:","+    \"\"\"Fails unless backtest() reads the field from the offline bundle.","+","+    backtest() reads scores and rewards a day past --eval-end; from the live API that is data from","+    after your cutoff.\"\"\"","+    if not os.environ.get(OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV):","+        raise SystemExit(","+            f\"{OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV} is not set, so backtest() would read the field from the live API, past \"","+            f\"--eval-end. The harness points it at the bundle in your snapshot; restore it.\"","+        )","+","+","+def store_root(asset: str) -> Path:","+    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.","+","+    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,","+    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do","+    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the","+    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"","+    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"","+","+","+def check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime, first_prompt: datetime) -> None:","+    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.","+","+    The context's days before the asset's first partition are not missing: the context holds them","+    as NaN. The days from the first prompt on are never exempt.","+    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and","+    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"","+    root = store_root(asset)","+    first = min((p.name for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\")), default=\"\")","+    holes_from = min(first, f\"date={first_prompt.date().isoformat()}.parquet\")","+    missing = []","+    cursor = start.date()","+    while cursor <= end.date():","+        name = f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\"","+        if name >= holes_from and not (root / name).exists():","+            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())","+        cursor += timedelta(days=1)","+    if missing:","+        raise SystemExit(","+            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"","+            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"","+            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only): it ends at the campaign's data_cutoff, and DATA.md gives \"","+            f\"each asset's first and last day. Choose --eval-end / --days so that the window and its \"","+            f\"CONTEXT_DAYS stay on days {root} holds.\"","+        )","+","+","+def prompt_times(","+    asset: str,","+    end: datetime,","+    days: int,","+    time_length: int,","+    time_increment: int,","+    cadence_minutes: int | None = None,","+) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:","+    \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the","+    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span.\"\"\"","+    first = end - timedelta(days=days)","+    if cadence_minutes is not None:","+        horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)","+        return list(pd.date_range(first - horizon, end - horizon, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"))","+    scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)","+    if scores.empty:","+        raise SystemExit(","+            f\"the offline bundle has no scored {asset} prompt for --time-length {time_length} in \"","+            f\"{first.date()} → {end.date()} (DATA.md gives its span); --crps-only scores CRPS alone \"","+            f\"on any window of the snapshot.\"","+        )","+    return sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())","+","+","+def generate(","+    asset: str,","+    times: list[pd.Timestamp],","+    out_dir: Path,","+    time_increment: int = 300,","+    time_length: int = 86_400,","+    num_simulations: int = 1000,","+) -> int:","+    # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises","+    # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never","+    # interpolate it away.","+    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), times[-1])","+    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+    head = 0","+    for t in times:","+        # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.","+        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, CONTEXT_DAYS)","+        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))","+        out = modeling.simulate(","+            asset=asset,","+            start_time=t.isoformat(),","+            time_increment=time_increment,","+            time_length=time_length,","+            num_simulations=num_simulations,","+            context_prices=context,","+        )","+        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]","+        record = {","+            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),","+            \"asset\": asset,","+            \"time_increment\": time_increment,","+            \"time_length\": time_length,","+            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),","+            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),","+            \"paths\": paths,","+        }","+        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"","+        (out_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(record))","+    if head:","+        print(","+            f\"warning: {asset} contexts start with up to {head / 1440:.1f} days of NaN, before its first price \"","+            f\"in the snapshot\"","+        )","+    return len(times)","+","+","+def print_event_split(prompts: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int) -> None:","+    \"\"\"Your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type","+    and over the prompts that hold none.\"\"\"","+    path = Path(os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV])","+    if not path.exists():","+        return","+    view = pd.read_parquet(path)","+    view = view[concerns(view, asset)]","+    scored = prompts[prompts[\"crps\"] > 0]  # -1 marks a prompt the backtester could not score","+    best = scored.groupby([\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])[\"crps\"].min().rename(\"best\")","+    ours = scored[scored[\"miner_id\"] == CANDIDATE_ID].join(best, on=[\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])","+    if ours.empty:","+        return","+    gap = ours[\"crps\"].to_numpy() / ours[\"best\"].to_numpy() - 1","+    starts = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"start_time\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy()","+    ends = starts + np.timedelta64(time_length, \"s\")","+    spans_any = np.zeros(len(ours), dtype=bool)","+    lines = []","+    for event, rows in view.groupby(\"event\"):","+        times = np.sort(pd.to_datetime(rows[\"time_utc\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy())","+        at = np.searchsorted(times, starts)","+        spans = (at < len(times)) & (times[np.minimum(at, len(times) - 1)] < ends)","+        spans_any |= spans","+        if spans.any():","+            lines.append(f\"  {event:<17} {spans.sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[spans].mean():+.2%}\")","+    if not spans_any.all():","+        lines.insert(0, f\"  {'no event':<17} {(~spans_any).sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[~spans_any].mean():+.2%}\")","+    print(\"event split (mean gap to each prompt's best miner):\")","+    print(\"\\n\".join(lines))","+","+","+def main() -> None:","+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","+    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")","+    ap.add_argument(","+        \"--num-simulations\",","+        type=int,","+        default=1000,","+        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"","+        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"","+        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",","+    )","+    ap.add_argument(","+        \"--cadence-minutes\",","+        type=int,","+        default=None,","+        help=\"answer an even grid every N minutes instead of the validator's own start times (with \"","+        \"--crps-only, 60 for 24h prompts and 10 for 1h by default). A cadence that divides an hour \"","+        \"puts every prompt on the round hour\",","+    )","+    ap.add_argument(","+        \"--latest-formula\",","+        action=\"store_true\",","+        help=\"score every crypto-1h prompt with the volatility term, as prompts are scored now, \"","+        \"including those scored before it went live. Field ranks before that day then compare \"","+        \"two formulas; CRPS does not\",","+    )","+    ap.add_argument(","+        \"--crps-only\",","+        action=\"store_true\",","+        help=\"CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid: no field and no rank, \"","+        \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",","+    )","+    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")","+    args = ap.parse_args()","+    if not args.crps_only:","+        require_offline_bundle()","+    ensure_workspace_cwd()","+    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)","+    cadence = args.cadence_minutes","+    if args.crps_only:","+        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]","+    times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)","+    # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far","+    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), end, times[0])","+    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))","+    try:","+        n = generate(","+            args.asset,","+            times,","+            out_dir,","+            time_increment=args.time_increment,","+            time_length=args.time_length,","+            num_simulations=args.num_simulations,","+        )","+        print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")","+        if args.crps_only:","+            result = score_crps(","+                miner_name=\"campaign\",","+                asset=args.asset,","+                time_length=args.time_length,","+                time_increment=args.time_increment,","+                predictions_dir=out_dir,","+            )","+            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)","+            return","+        result = backtest(","+            miner_name=\"campaign\",","+            asset=args.asset,","+            time_length=args.time_length,","+            time_increment=args.time_increment,","+            n_backtest_days=args.days,","+            predictions_dir=out_dir,","+            eval_end=end,","+            latest_formula=args.latest_formula,","+            match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,","+        )","+        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)","+        if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):","+            print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)","+    finally:","+        if args.keep_predictions:","+            print(f\"predictions kept in {out_dir}\")","+        else:","+            shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)","+","+","+if __name__ == \"__main__\":","+    main()"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/research/starter_eval/modeling.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":34,"lines":["+\"\"\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.","+","+This is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.","+Contract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has","+time_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.","+\"\"\"","+","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import numpy as np","+","+# Days of minute history simulate() receives as context_prices: a plain int from 3 to 30.","+CONTEXT_DAYS = 7","+","+","+def simulate(","+    asset: str,","+    start_time,","+    time_increment: int = 300,","+    time_length: int = 86_400,","+    num_simulations: int = 1000,","+    context_prices=None,","+):","+    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1","+    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].dropna()","+    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])","+    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))","+    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]","+    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3","+    rng = np.random.default_rng()","+    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))","+    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0","+    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))","+    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/research/official_eval.sh","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":11,"lines":["+#!/bin/bash","+# Official numbers: agent/predict.py (synth-lib backtest, 1000 paths, validator prompt times),","+# one run per (configuration, asset), 10 days of scored prompts before EVAL_END.","+# usage: official_eval.sh <predict.py path> <out dir> [eval_end] [days]","+PRED=$1; OUT=$2; END=${3:-2026-11-08}; DAYS=${4:-10}","+mkdir -p $OUT","+cd /workspace","+run() { uv run $PRED --asset $1 --days $DAYS --eval-end $END $2 > $OUT/$3_$1.log 2>&1; }","+for a in BTC ETH SOL XRP HYPE; do run $a \"\" crypto-24h & done; wait","+for a in XAU NVDAX GOOGLX TSLAX AAPLX WTIOIL SPCX SP500; do run $a \"\" com-equ-24h & done; wait","+for a in BTC ETH SOL XRP HYPE; do run $a \"--time-length 3600 --time-increment 60\" crypto-1h & done; wait"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/journal.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":151,"oldLines":3,"newStart":151,"newLines":12,"lines":["   (B); crypto -0.04/+0.07 (A), +0.01/+0.03 (B). The fitted shape (exponent 1) is right."," - weekend variance x0.8 / x1.25: com-equ -0.06/+0.13 (A), -0.02/+0.07 (B, only 3/8 cells better","   at 0.8); crypto +0.02/+0.08, 0.00/+0.10. Weekend level right within ~10%. No change.","+","+## Iteration 12 — the Friday-afternoon prompts (worst com-equ prompts in window C)","+Worst prompts vs the field median in C are SP500/AAPLX prompts starting Friday 16:00-23:00 NY:","++30-40%. Inspected SP500 Fri 11-06 16:15 NY: model sigma 3.3-4.1 bp across the horizon,","+realised 0.45-1.8 bp — the hot Friday session (last-6h rms 10 bp) inflated the level, and the","+weekend does not follow it.","+- weekend steps use slow-heavy EWMA weights ([0,.3,.7] or [0,0,1]) for every prompt: A com-equ","+  +0.06/+0.15%, crypto +0.56/+1.43%; B +0.05/+0.13%, crypto +0.01/+0.05%; C -0.02/-0.05%. Much","+  worse: inside a weekend, the weekend's own recent minutes are the best information. Discard."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/workspace/agent/research/starter_eval/predict.py","/workspace/agent/research/starter_eval/modeling.py","/workspace/agent/research/official_eval.sh","/workspace/agent/journal.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011ykLPkABVncvKVtakWKrXV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
